## Recommended Pattern: Scoped Service + Event Notification

Given per-page interactivity with a static layout, here's the approach:

### Key insight

Your layout is static SSR, so `CascadingValue` won't propagate changes reactively. Instead:

1. **Scoped service** (`AddScoped<ThemeService>`) — in Blazor Server, "scoped" = per-circuit, giving each user independent state.
2. **Event-based notification** — the service exposes an `OnChange` event; consuming components subscribe and call `StateHasChanged()`.
3. **Interactive islands in the static layout** — mark the header's theme indicator with `@rendermode="InteractiveServer"` so it can subscribe to changes even though `MainLayout` itself is static.

### Architecture

```
┌─ MainLayout (Static SSR) ─────────────────────────┐
│                                                     │
│  ┌─ ThemeIndicator.razor (@rendermode Server) ──┐  │
│  │  Injects ThemeService, subscribes OnChange   │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                     │
│  ┌─ @Body (per-page Interactive Server) ────────┐  │
│  │  Components inject ThemeService,             │  │
│  │  read/write theme, subscribe OnChange        │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Why this works for each requirement

| # | Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Any component reads/writes theme | All inject the same scoped instance |
| 2 | Changes propagate everywhere | `OnChange` event → `StateHasChanged()` |
| 3 | Settings page updates header | Same service instance, same event |
| 4 | Per-user isolation | `AddScoped` = per-circuit in Server mode |
| 5 | Persists across enhanced nav | Circuit (and its scoped services) survives navigation |

### Implementation skeleton

**ThemeService.cs** — notify subscribers on mutation:
```csharp
public class ThemeService
{
    public ThemeMode Theme { get; private set; } = ThemeMode.System;
    public string AccentColor { get; private set; } = "#0078d4";

    public event Action? OnChange;

    public void SetTheme(ThemeMode mode)
    {
        Theme = mode;
        OnChange?.Invoke();
    }

    public void SetAccentColor(string color)
    {
        AccentColor = color;
        OnChange?.Invoke();
    }
}
```

**Any consuming component** — subscribe/unsubscribe:
```razor
@implements IDisposable
@inject ThemeService Theme

<div style="color: @Theme.AccentColor">Current: @Theme.Theme</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
}
```

**In the static layout**, the indicator must be an interactive island:
```razor
<!-- MainLayout.razor (no @rendermode) -->
<header>
    <ThemeIndicator @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</header>
```

**Registration:**
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<ThemeService>();
```

This is the standard pattern for app-wide mutable state in per-page Interactive Server apps. Want me to scaffold this into your project?
